```js
async function getUser(id) {
  const rows = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);
  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');
  return rows[0];
}
```

Callers use `try/catch` or `.catch()` instead of checking the `err` argument. Assumes `db.query` returns a promise — if it's still callback-only, wrap it first with `util.promisify(db.query)`.
